  "notes": "Passive conveyor, flow -X, four actual 40x40 L-feet on the tabletop. Ten galvanised D30 x 316 hollow steel rollers, 50 mm pitch, top 50 mm; blue #1E4C9A real 40x20x2 C-channels with top at 40 mm preserve the 10 mm hand clearance. Thin sheet edges use 0.4-0.45 mm 3-segment radii so the 2 mm walls survive; the stop uses 2 mm radii. SPEC CONFLICT: a single convex collider cannot represent the 18x36 mm open C-channel within the general 1 mm rule. Each side therefore has three convex web/flange boxes, rather than one hull filling its groove. Feet, fixed axles and support ears also have individual convex proxies. Each rotating roller has exactly one 16-sided cylinder collider; its polygon vertices lie on the nominal D30 circle. The removable 320Y x 20X x 30Z stop has its top 20 mm above the rollers and is fitted immediately outside the -X end of the 480 mm side channels, so the complete fitted conveyor is exactly 500 mm long. The ten rollers occupy a 480 mm envelope including their radii. The stop is outboard of that envelope to avoid intersecting the first roller. Feet give 440 mm overall width; the internal clear width remains 320. All meshes, proxies and hinge anchors have been shifted +10 mm X together to centre the fitted assembly. Remove the end_stop part for the stop_removed variant. Continuous Y hinges use limited=false, continuous=true, damping=0.001 and frictionloss=0. The finite +/-pi range is present only for the existing schema; simulation must respect limited=false and allow unlimited rotation. Identical translated roller meshes retain identical UVs and reuse the actual roller_00 2048px Cycles bake in ten separate PNG files. Listed masses are reasonable modelling estimates because no equipment masses were specified. Metres, Z up, front -X; identity object transforms and one common prop frame for all parts. 30-degree split smoothing, weighted normals, triangulated OBJ with normals. Nonoverlapping Smart UV 66-degree atlases, 0.01 island margins. Albedo = CPU Cycles 64-sample diffuse COLOR * (0.4 + 0.6 * AO), 8-bit sRGB, without direct lighting or highlights. Full procedural Principled PBR and original label UVs are packed in source.blend. Preview: 1024 square, CPU Cycles 64, neutral grey, three area lights, front-left above. Generated with Blender 5.2.0 LTS. Task 13 compact OBJ exception: positions use 5 decimal metres where safe; necessary vertices retain up to 6 decimals to preserve nonzero triangles, strict collision convexity and the 0.005 mm Euclidean movement bound. Independent fixed-5 rounding cannot satisfy all three. Normals/UVs use 4 decimals; every original triangle, position index and per-corner attribute value is retained. Equal rounded UV records share indices and visual OBJ indices use shorter equivalent relative notation. No collision remeshing, reindexing or simplification. Task 13 delivery: baked albedos are Lanczos-downsampled to at most 1024 px except the unchanged-resolution factory-floor repeat tile; previews are 512 square. PNG encoding uses RGB8 or reviewed 256-colour Floyd-Steinberg palettes; source artwork pixels and source.blend are retained. Shared PNG paths resolve from this prop folder.",
